msgid "Windows Development Environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/development/mavdevenvwindows.rst:5
#: 58b52f576f2e4be2a96cd16e22a6c14c
msgid "You will need to have `Python <http://www.python.org>`_ 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/development/mavdevenvwindows.rst:7
#: b56ed3265c7a4282b63d55f79c84584f
msgid "It is assumed that Python and pip are on the system path. If not, see `here <https://datatofish.com/add-python-to-windows-path/>`_ for instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/development/mavdevenvwindows.rst:9
#: 0d488b8504164bec9d5dc5226c56153b
msgid "To install the required libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/development/mavdevenvwindows.rst:17
#: dda28588b20b4f8aaace39377e4cacdc
msgid "Download the MAVProxy `source <https://github.com/ArduPilot/MAVProxy>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/development/mavdevenvwindows.rst:19
#: 98337694f02f46a99a741f1c311f55f4
msgid "After making the desired changes, MAVProxy is required to be compiled into the Python directory (the modules won't work otherwise). This needs to happen after any changes to the source code. This can be done by running the :file:`./MAVProxy/MAVProxyWinUSB.bat` or :file:`./MAVProxy/MAVProxyWinLAN.bat` file. This will perform the necessary build actions and then run MAVProxy. Some of the details in the batch files (port numbers, etc) may need to be altered to match the user's system configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/development/mavdevenvwindows.rst:28
#: 60e2c05bca7e4989aded62997b756cfb
msgid "To create a one-click windows installer for MAVProxy, run ``MAVProxyWinBuild.bat```, which is in the ``./windows`` directory. The installer will be created in the ``./windows/output`` directory. The `Inno Setup <http://www.jrsoftware.org/isdl.php#stable>`_ program will be required for this process and is assumed to be installed in the ``C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Inno Setup 6\\`` folder"
msgstr ""
